{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1490520588,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyMTcwMzk1MDQ=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1442","origin":"github"},"title":"Observations on git annex metadata behavior (e.g. git-annex will not error when setting metadata of a non-annexed file or non-existing path)","message":"Not sure yet if this is a feature or a bug. For now just collecting observations:\n\nTest case: a repo with one file in git and one (later two and three) in annex:\n\n````\n% git init \u0026\u0026 git annex init\nInitialized empty Git repository in /tmp/meta/.git/\ninit  ok\n(recording state in git...)\n% echo \"123\" \u003e in_git \u0026\u0026 git add in_git \u0026\u0026 git commit -m 'ingit'\n[master (root-commit) 44725bd] ingit\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)\n create mode 100644 in_git\n% echo \"456\" \u003e in_annex \u0026\u0026 git annex add in_annex \u0026\u0026 git commit -m 'inannex'   \nadd in_annex ok\n(recording state in git...)\n[master 9496a29] inannex\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)\n create mode 120000 in_annex\n````\n\nNo error code for read access, just output different:\n\n````\n% git annex metadata --json in_git\n% git annex metadata --json in_annex\n{\"command\":\"metadata\",\"note\":\"\",\"success\":true,\"key\":\"SHA256E-s4--cdfba543ee8ef7fdb3d8b587648cc22dd792bbd6272cc5447307c7c106c2374c\",\"file\":\"in_annex\",\"fields\":{}}\n````\n\nDirectory as path argument refers to all content\n\n````\ngit annex metadata --json .\n{\"command\":\"metadata\",\"note\":\"\",\"success\":true,\"key\":\"SHA256E-s4--cdfba543ee8ef7fdb3d8b587648cc22dd792bbd6272cc5447307c7c106c2374c\",\"file\":\"in_annex\",\"fields\":{}}\n````\n\nSilently ignores metadata `set` for files in Git (I guess that makes it easier to recursively set metadata in mixed repos):\n\n````\n% git annex metadata in_git -s some=value\n% git annex metadata --json in_annex -s some=value\n{\"command\":\"metadata\",\"note\":\"lastchanged=2017-03-26@09-10-41\\nsome=value\\nsome-lastchanged=2017-03-26@09-10-41\\n\",\"success\":true,\"key\":\"SHA256E-s4--cdfba543ee8ef7fdb3d8b587648cc22dd792bbd6272cc5447307c7c106c2374c\",\"file\":\"in_annex\",\"fields\":{\"some\":[\"value\"],\"lastchanged\":[\"2017-03-26@09-10-41\"],\"some-lastchanged\":[\"2017-03-26@09-10-41\"]}}\n````\n\nRequired switch for recursive `metadata set`, but with `--force` ignored file in Git without error.\n\n````\n% echo \"789\" \u003e in_annex2 \u0026\u0026 git annex add in_annex2 \u0026\u0026 git commit -m 'inannex'\n% git annex metadata --json . -s someother=value2\ngit-annex: Not recursively setting metadata. Use --force to do that.\n1 % git annex metadata --force --json . -s someother=value2\n{\"command\":\"metadata\",\"note\":\"lastchanged=2017-03-26@09-14-03\\nsome=value\\nsome-lastchanged=2017-03-26@09-10-41\\nsomeother=value2\\nsomeother-lastchanged=2017-03-26@09-14-03\\n\",\"success\":true,\"key\":\"SHA256E-s4--cdfba543ee8ef7fdb3d8b587648cc22dd792bbd6272cc5447307c7c106c2374c\",\"file\":\"in_annex\",\"fields\":{\"some\":[\"value\"],\"someother-lastchanged\":[\"2017-03-26@09-14-03\"],\"someother\":[\"value2\"],\"lastchanged\":[\"2017-03-26@09-14-03\"],\"some-lastchanged\":[\"2017-03-26@09-10-41\"]}}\n{\"command\":\"metadata\",\"note\":\"lastchanged=2017-03-26@09-14-03\\nsomeother=value2\\nsomeother-lastchanged=2017-03-26@09-14-03\\n\",\"success\":true,\"key\":\"SHA256E-s4--d928266e89b1da2263838e86df3a430548ca1768bedbc9d4b20f9e370d5518df\",\"file\":\"in_annex2\",\"fields\":{\"someother-lastchanged\":[\"2017-03-26@09-14-03\"],\"someother\":[\"value2\"],\"lastchanged\":[\"2017-03-26@09-14-03\"]}}\n````\n\n`--json` has no effect when used together with `--get-field`:\n\n````\n% git annex metadata --json -g someother\nvalue2\nvalue2\n````\n\nMetadata is `set` per annex key, not per file, even if a file argument is given:\n\n````\n% git annex lookupkey in_annex in_annex_samekey \nSHA256E-s4--cdfba543ee8ef7fdb3d8b587648cc22dd792bbd6272cc5447307c7c106c2374c\nSHA256E-s4--cdfba543ee8ef7fdb3d8b587648cc22dd792bbd6272cc5447307c7c106c2374c\n% git annex metadata in_annex -s unique=yes\nmetadata in_annex \n  lastchanged=2017-03-26@09-22-07\n  some=value\n  some-lastchanged=2017-03-26@09-10-41\n  someother=value2\n  someother-lastchanged=2017-03-26@09-14-03\n  unique=yes\n  unique-lastchanged=2017-03-26@09-22-07\nok\n(recording state in git...)\n% git annex metadata -g unique\nyes\nyes\n````\n\nWhen an update changes the annex key of a file, no metadata is lost\n\n````\n% git annex unlock in_annex\nunlock in_annex (copying...) ok\n% echo \"more\" \u003e\u003e in_annex\n% git annex add in_annex\nadd in_annex ok\n(recording state in git...)\n% git commit -m update\n[master 77f21e1] update\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)\n% git annex lookupkey in_annex in_annex_samekey\nSHA256E-s9--d9375e7eeb21c8856728988bd073c546380cb07bd0b9c4b77f05e7d2799738e0\nSHA256E-s4--cdfba543ee8ef7fdb3d8b587648cc22dd792bbd6272cc5447307c7c106c2374c\n% git annex metadata in_annex\nmetadata in_annex \n  lastchanged=2017-03-26@09-22-07\n  some=value\n  some-lastchanged=2017-03-26@09-10-41\n  someother=value2\n  someother-lastchanged=2017-03-26@09-14-03\n  unique=yes\n  unique-lastchanged=2017-03-26@09-22-07\nok\n% git annex metadata in_annex -s moreunique=yes\nmetadata in_annex \n  lastchanged=2017-03-26@09-41-26\n  moreunique=yes\n  moreunique-lastchanged=2017-03-26@09-41-26\n  some=value\n  some-lastchanged=2017-03-26@09-10-41\n  someother=value2\n  someother-lastchanged=2017-03-26@09-14-03\n  unique=yes\n  unique-lastchanged=2017-03-26@09-22-07\nok\n(recording state in git...)\n% git annex metadata -g moreunique\nyes\n````\n\nNo error when setting metadata of non-existing paths (but errors on `get`) -- I cannot think of a reason why this is a good thing (TM):\n\n````\n% git annex metadata --json thinair\ngit-annex: thinair not found\ngit-annex: metadata: 1 failed\n1 % git annex metadata --json thinair -s wannabe=here\n% git annex metadata --json thinair\ngit-annex: thinair not found\ngit-annex: metadata: 1 failed\n1 \n````","files":null}]}